# BrickBasket Frontend — example environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values as needed. Every
# variable below is safe to expose to the browser (Next.js ships anything
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ to the client bundle) — see docs/ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md
# for the always-current, authoritative list.
#
# No variable here is required to run this app locally. No secret, API key,
# or backend credential belongs in this file, in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable,
# or committed to this repository at all.

# Production site URL, used for metadataBase/Open Graph tags in
# src/app/layout.tsx. Falls back to a placeholder domain if unset — see
# docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md #17. Set to the real production domain before launch.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.brickbasket.co.in

# Not yet used by any code in this repository — there is no backend to point
# at yet. Staged here for when one exists: src/lib/api/http-client.ts already
# reads this exact variable name. Uncomment and set once a real backend is
# deployed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.brickbasket.co.in
